               * so the caller is talking about a real exchange; whether the
               * proof was malformed, the wrong length or simply wrong is its
               * own business and telling it apart helps nobody but a guesser.
* 25 Sep 26 SD Core Solo - RULING 19: the proof is checked against the user's
*   StoredKey and, only if that fails, against $GLOBAL's (vb.scram.first kept
*   it only when it shares the salt).  scram.check.proof is the single check
*   that used to stand here, run once per key; a global match signs with the
*   global ServerKey and marks the session for K$ADMINISTRATOR below.
